SnappyMail release-signing public key — PROVISIONAL, see TODO.md

    uid          SnappyMail <releases@snappymail.eu>
    fingerprint  1016 E470 7914 5542 F8BA  1335 4820 8BA1 3290 F3EB
    algorithm    ed25519 (EdDSA), key created 2022-02-16

Where this key comes from, and what is still missing:

  * Fetched from keyserver.ubuntu.com, which is independent of the
    server that serves the release tarballs. The key was uploaded there
    in February 2022, more than two years before the signature it
    verifies was made (2024-10-09), so whoever controls the download
    server today could not have planted it retroactively.

  * Verified: this key produces `Good signature` on
    snappymail-2.38.2.tar.gz against its detached .asc signature.

  * NOT yet done: the fingerprint above is not confirmed against a
    statement published by the SnappyMail project itself. snappymail.eu
    did not respond when this key was taken in, and neither the GitHub
    README nor the release notes state a fingerprint. Until that
    confirmation exists, this pinning protects against a tampered or
    corrupted tarball on the download path; it does not prove that the
    key belongs to the SnappyMail maintainer.

Re-check when snappymail.eu is reachable again (the task is in
TODO.md): compare the fingerprint with the published value and replace
this note with the source that confirmed it.

Any downgrade of this file back to a placeholder must be treated as a
security incident: it disables SnappyMail release-signature verification
across every future build.

